While upgrading our kafka clusters to new operating systems I switched to dynamic voter configuration and removed controller instances with {{/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh}} and the {{remove-controller}} subcommand. Inspecting the cluster with {{describe}} only shows the actual running nodes.
Now during the update to 4.2.0, the final metadata upgrade step complains about
{code:java}
Could not upgrade eligible.leader.replicas.version to 1. The update failed for all features since the following feature had an error: Invalid update version 29 for feature metadata.version. Controller 351 only supports versions 7-27{code}
with 351 being an ID of an already removed controller. Inspecting a snapshot with {{/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-metadata-shell.sh}} indeed shows all controller ids of already removed controllers:
{code:java}
>> ls image/cluster/controllers/
158 206 351 584 611 686 {code}
while other tools only show the expected nodes:
{code:java}
~$ /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh --bootstrap-controller localhost:9093 describe --replication --human-readable
NodeId DirectoryId LogEndOffset Lag LastFetchTimestamp LastCaughtUpTimestamp Status 
158 2gsvOvnT7urpZcA_-LUy5w 196823524 0 7 ms ago 8 ms ago Leader 
611 27Ii-xdAZ7ReQBLsvvJb0A 196823524 0 348 ms ago 348 ms ago Follower 
206 Q7X9o3XbKxk_3tz4T8torg 196823524 0 348 ms ago 348 ms ago Follower 
226 7n6aedUEuytkqhBnbe7ESw 196823524 0 348 ms ago 348 ms ago Observer 
181 tZ17VQ8cYpf7R-LyAQWf2w 196823524 0 349 ms ago 349 ms ago Observer 
299 P4qXt3K0G5Qg_7w_UdvaNA 196823524 0 348 ms ago 348 ms ago Observer 
290 bA0pqZFsUa45lRTB6bS4bg 196823524 0 348 ms ago 348 ms ago Observer 
293 Av_12222lURKVYVt-aNKOQ 196823524 0 348 ms ago 348 ms ago Observer 
485 glENIgkIng1MYDF8HxxoDQ 196823524 0 349 ms ago 350 ms ago Observer {code}
Grepping through {{bin/kafka-dump-log.sh --cluster-metadata-decoder}} only shows the expected three {{REGISTER_CONTROLLER_RECORD}} entries.

Is there any clear path for removing those stale nodes?

comments.body:
Ok here is in more detail what we did:

 

{{In the image apache/kafka:4.3.1 }}

{{I prepared 2 files}}
 * {{A controller file looking exactly like one of my running cluster}}

 ** {{I set the node id to the one I want to "fake"}}

 ** {{{}and I use the same _c_{}}}{_}ontroller.quorum.bootstrap.servers{_} as my running cluster

 * A command properties file with
 ** the needed admin connexion user and password
 ** the needed config from the controller configuration to run the register command

 

then I start image with 
{code:java}
docker run -it -u 0:0 --name host_name  --hostname host_name kafka-dev:4.3.1 {code}
 


Then format the controller{{{}{}}}

 
{code:java}
/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-storage.sh format --cluster-id CLUSTER_ID --initial-controllers "ID1@HOTS1:9090:FOLDER_ID_1,ID2@HOTS3:9090:FOLDER_ID_2" --config /opt/kafka/config/controller.properties {code}
 

then a start of kafka
{code:java}
/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-server-start.sh /opt/kafka/config/controller.properties {code}

then a register:
{code:java}
/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh --command-config /opt/kafka/config/command.properties --bootstrap-server DOCKER_HOST_NAME:9090 add-controller {code}

hope this helps

